    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8cc320c9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of armed, masked individuals sitting on the ground, with firearms laid out in front of them. The overlaid text reads: 'i was going to make a joke about us but they always blow up in your face.' The visual material (armed combatants) is juxtaposed with the text to imply that the group being referenced (likely a specific ethnic, religious, or national group) is inherently dangerous or prone to violence. This framing is a form of hate speech, as it uses the image of armed militants to stereotype and dehumanize a group, suggesting they are inherently violent and unpredictable. The meme is designed to provoke fear or hostility toward the group it references, fitting the definition of a hateful meme. The intent is to delegitimize or demonize the group by associating them with terrorism and violence, which is a harmful and hateful portrayal.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2bd519bc"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
