    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_21747248",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "hateful_joke_structure",
      "label": "Hateful Joke Structure",
      "description": "The meme uses a structure where the speaker claims to be making a joke about 'us' (the group being targeted), but then immediately pivots to a violent outcome ('they always blow up in your face'), which is a rhetorical device used to express hatred or fear toward the group. This structure is a form of hate speech that relies on the audience understanding the targeted group.",
